  "title": "sambil — while",
  "pattern": "A sambil B · Sambil B, A",
  "explanation": "sambil joins two things one person does at the same time. The main activity comes first and the background one after sambil: Saya suka masak sambil dengar musik. — I like cooking while listening to music. The same person does both, so there's no second subject after sambil. It can also start the sentence: Sambil menunggu, kita minum kopi dulu.",
  "natural": "Everyday, in any register: habits, doing two things at once, and juggling work and study (kerja sambil kuliah).",
  "stiff": "Not for two different people: Saya masak sambil dia mandi is wrong. Say Saya masak waktu dia mandi (I cooked while he had a shower).",
